WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.048
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.318 --> 00:54.284
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:55.160 --> 00:56.578
JONGNO PAWNSHOP

4
00:57.078 --> 00:57.912
EPISODE 3

5
00:57.996 --> 00:59.330
What, a pickpocket?

6
01:00.081 --> 01:02.250
I have no idea what you're talking about.

7
01:02.333 --> 01:05.503
That's right. She's my customer.

8
01:08.214 --> 01:09.048
Here.

9
01:09.132 --> 01:11.092
She came to pawn this.

10
01:14.971 --> 01:15.930
Then what is this?

11
01:17.098 --> 01:19.601
My father gave me a wallet for my graduation gift.

12
01:19.684 --> 01:21.769
It looks just like that wallet.

13
01:21.853 --> 01:22.687
Let me see.

14
01:24.189 --> 01:25.356
There's some writing on the wallet.

15
01:26.024 --> 01:28.818
"Sato Hideo."

16
01:28.902 --> 01:30.653
That name sounds familiar.

17
01:30.737 --> 01:31.946
What do you think?

18
01:33.823 --> 01:36.284
Did you say you were looking for Jongno Pawnshop?

19
01:37.035 --> 01:40.038
That's too bad. This isn't the Jongno Pawnshop.

20
01:40.121 --> 01:42.207
Stop lying. I'm not falling for it again.

21
01:42.290 --> 01:45.168
I'm telling you, it's not. Go check the sign outside.

22
01:45.251 --> 01:46.711
I did see the sign outside.

23
01:46.794 --> 01:48.796
You're trying to get me out so you can run away.

24
01:48.880 --> 01:50.006
You think I don't know that?

25
01:50.089 --> 01:52.217
I'm not lying. This is…

26
01:52.300 --> 01:53.760
THE FIRST JONGNO PAWNSHOP

27
01:53.843 --> 01:54.719
"The First."

28
01:54.802 --> 01:57.180
This is "The First Jongno Pawnshop."

29
01:57.263 --> 01:59.182
Though it opened only three years ago.

30
01:59.265 --> 02:00.099
That's right.

31
02:00.183 --> 02:03.144
It's the Jongno Pawnshop with "The First" in its name.

32
02:03.978 --> 02:07.190
Do you know how many pawnshops there are around Jongno?

33
02:07.273 --> 02:08.358
There must be dozens.

34
02:08.441 --> 02:10.693
There are probably more than ten just down the alley--

35
02:12.070 --> 02:14.322
I don't care if this is the first one or not.

36
02:14.405 --> 02:16.115
Enough with the lies.

37
02:19.118 --> 02:20.787
I'll give you one last chance.

38
02:21.579 --> 02:23.206
Give it to me while I'm being nice.

39
02:27.752 --> 02:30.838
Honestly, I don't know what you want from me.

40
02:30.922 --> 02:32.882
I said this is your last chance.

41
02:34.133 --> 02:35.843
Hands in the air!

42
02:38.304 --> 02:40.014
Don't move! Hands up!

43
02:41.307 --> 02:42.976
Move! Bring everyone down.

44
02:45.186 --> 02:46.229
Damn it.

45
02:47.188 --> 02:49.107
I can't believe you called the police over this.

46
02:49.190 --> 02:51.276
Being the inspector general's son must be nice.

47
02:52.777 --> 02:54.028
Why are your hands up?

48
02:54.612 --> 02:55.571
I didn't call them.

49
02:55.655 --> 02:56.823
You there.

50
02:57.740 --> 02:58.574
Quiet!

51
03:00.451 --> 03:03.579
I'm Sato Hideo, an interpreter trainee at the Government-General of Joseon.

52
03:03.663 --> 03:04.872
Freeze.

53
03:06.916 --> 03:09.836
I was going to show you my Government-General ID.

54
03:17.802 --> 03:20.013
An interpreter trainee for the Government-General?

55
03:20.096 --> 03:21.556
Yes, my name is Sato Hideo.

56
03:24.017 --> 03:26.227
I didn't want to mention this,

57
03:26.728 --> 03:29.480
but Sato Shinichi, the inspector general, is my father.

58
03:30.356 --> 03:31.190
That's right.

59
03:32.275 --> 03:33.901
I saw him at Keijo Station.

60
03:36.362 --> 03:38.489
Forgive me, I didn't realize who you were!

61
03:39.198 --> 03:40.742
Come on. Put the guns down!

62
03:40.825 --> 03:42.243
-Yes, sir. Sorry! -I'm sorry!

63
03:44.329 --> 03:45.246
It's fine.

64
03:46.622 --> 03:49.208
You sure know how to use your father's influence.

65
03:49.292 --> 03:51.627
It really is nice being the inspector general's son.

66
03:55.214 --> 03:56.883
Anyway, what's going on?

67
03:56.966 --> 04:00.345
We're looking for the Gugukdan members who targeted your father yesterday.

68
04:00.428 --> 04:02.597
I was there myself.

69
04:02.680 --> 04:04.098
By the Gugukdan,

70
04:04.182 --> 04:06.726
do you mean the organization based in Shanghai?

71
04:06.809 --> 04:08.394
Was that man with the Gugukdan?

72
04:08.478 --> 04:09.645
Yes.

73
04:09.729 --> 04:12.190
We got a tip-off that a Gugukdan member recently came to Keijo

74
04:12.273 --> 04:14.400
and headed for Jongno, so we're after him.

75
04:15.651 --> 04:16.986
Are you the innkeeper?

76
04:17.070 --> 04:19.447
If you're hiding someone from the Gugukdan, tell me now!

77
04:19.530 --> 04:21.741
Wait, wait. Shoot…

78
04:21.824 --> 04:23.493
I mean, don't shoot.

79
04:23.576 --> 04:25.161
Wait a moment. What's he saying?

80
04:27.246 --> 04:28.206
I can interpret.

81
04:31.334 --> 04:32.168
So…

82
04:32.752 --> 04:36.297
He's asking if you're hiding a Gugukdan independence fighter here.

83
04:36.381 --> 04:38.925
An independence fighter? That's ridiculous.

84
04:39.008 --> 04:40.176
Absolutely not.

85
04:40.259 --> 04:41.594
This inn…

86
04:41.677 --> 04:43.054
This place…

87
04:43.137 --> 04:45.014
…has no ties to the independence movement.

88
04:45.098 --> 04:46.641
…isn't tied to the movement.

89
04:46.724 --> 04:49.143
This place is the…

90
04:49.227 --> 04:51.729
Right, it's the watermill in Jongno.

91
04:52.480 --> 04:53.606
It's the watermill.

92
04:53.689 --> 04:55.233
What are you babbling about? Mill?

93
04:55.316 --> 04:56.609
"Mill"?

94
04:56.692 --> 04:59.362
Yes, a watermill. Do they know what that means around here?

95
04:59.445 --> 05:01.864
-Translate that for me. I'll explain. -What?

96
05:01.948 --> 05:05.827
A watermill is where the wheel starts turning, and the pounding begins--

97
05:05.910 --> 05:07.286
Hold on!

98
05:07.370 --> 05:08.871
I'll explain it myself.

99
05:08.955 --> 05:09.872
Well…

100
05:09.956 --> 05:11.082
This inn is a place

101
05:12.208 --> 05:16.254
mostly used by young men and women during the day.

102
05:16.337 --> 05:18.131
What do they do in broad daylight?

103
05:18.214 --> 05:19.882
Are independence fighters hiding here?

104
05:19.966 --> 05:21.134
No, that's not it!

105
05:21.217 --> 05:22.135
What?

106
05:22.218 --> 05:23.928
Don't they have watermills in Japan?

107
05:24.011 --> 05:24.971
This is where…

108
05:27.682 --> 05:30.935
people come in pairs to play sports.

109
05:31.018 --> 05:31.978
What?

110
05:32.687 --> 05:34.772
Sports in pairs?

111
05:34.856 --> 05:36.941
Yes, sports.

112
05:45.074 --> 05:46.075
I get it.

113
05:49.120 --> 05:51.456
Still, check their IDs. Search the place.

114
05:51.539 --> 05:53.166
-Yes, sir! -They'll check IDs.

115
05:53.249 --> 05:54.167
What?

116
05:55.877 --> 05:56.919
Okay.

117
06:00.465 --> 06:03.217
If I may ask, Mr. Sato, what were you doing here?

118
06:04.218 --> 06:05.178
Who is she?

119
06:08.514 --> 06:09.474
She's…

120
06:09.557 --> 06:10.683
If I get arrested,

121
06:11.684 --> 06:14.270
you'll never find that pawn ticket.

122
06:15.563 --> 06:18.107
How did you know it was a pawn ticket?

123
06:18.191 --> 06:19.775
I never told you what it was.

124
06:21.152 --> 06:22.069
This woman…

125
06:22.153 --> 06:24.947
Sin Tae-jin! Who… is that?

126
06:25.531 --> 06:26.866
The owner of that pawn ticket.

127
06:30.870 --> 06:33.372
Does the inspector general know him?

128
06:33.456 --> 06:34.916
I want to know all of a sudden.

129
06:36.834 --> 06:38.085
This lady…

130
06:40.796 --> 06:41.797
is here with me.

131
06:43.466 --> 06:44.342
With you?

132
06:45.468 --> 06:46.302
That's right.

133
06:47.136 --> 06:48.387
We're a pair.

134
06:49.972 --> 06:51.390
She's my partner in sports.

135
06:53.768 --> 06:55.394
Oh, your "partner in sports."

136
06:56.479 --> 06:59.607
I'm sorry, I was being slow. My apologies.

137
07:00.191 --> 07:01.651
-Put the gun down. -Yes, sir.

138
07:01.734 --> 07:04.153
What did you just tell them?

139
07:04.237 --> 07:05.112
Let go, will you?

140
07:05.196 --> 07:07.740
You'd better cooperate with me for now.

141
07:08.407 --> 07:09.617
Thank you.

142
07:09.700 --> 07:11.202
Please keep this brief.

143
07:11.285 --> 07:12.453
I'm in a bit of a rush.

144
07:12.537 --> 07:14.205
Yes, sir, I understand.

145
07:14.288 --> 07:17.208
I'd appreciate it if you kept this

146
07:18.543 --> 07:19.418
just between us.

147
07:19.502 --> 07:21.170
Certainly.

148
07:21.254 --> 07:23.506
We'll wrap up the search quickly.

149
07:23.589 --> 07:26.467
The first half, the second half, and even overtime.

150
07:26.551 --> 07:28.386
I hope you enjoy the whole game!

151
07:29.136 --> 07:30.054
Hurry up!

152
07:31.973 --> 07:32.807
See?

153
07:35.768 --> 07:38.312
Once the search is over, let's settle our business.

154
07:39.230 --> 07:40.064
All right?

155
07:43.526 --> 07:44.777
We caught someone suspicious.

156
07:45.778 --> 07:47.697
He's outside. Come have a look.

157
07:49.490 --> 07:50.575
Mr. Sato.

158
07:50.658 --> 07:53.661
Since you were at the scene last night, you must have seen the suspect.

159
07:53.744 --> 07:55.246
Please see if you can identify him.

160
07:57.707 --> 07:58.583
Sure.

161
08:01.294 --> 08:03.045
I'll be right back.

162
08:03.129 --> 08:05.756
Don't even think about running off.

163
08:05.840 --> 08:07.967
You're smart enough to know this situation, right?

164
08:08.676 --> 08:10.636
-Yes. -Good to know.

165
08:11.387 --> 08:12.388
If you'll excuse me.

166
08:25.318 --> 08:27.028
This is driving me crazy, darn it.

167
08:29.739 --> 08:30.573
Excuse me.

168
08:31.365 --> 08:32.366
Excuse me?

169
08:32.950 --> 08:35.369
-Yes? -What's going on here?

170
08:36.954 --> 08:40.333
Well, last night…

171
08:46.172 --> 08:47.298
The thing is…

172
08:52.094 --> 08:52.970
It's not him.

173
08:54.263 --> 08:56.432
He doesn't even fit the age profile.

174
08:56.515 --> 08:58.809
-Take him to the Jongno Station. -Yes, sir!

175
09:00.770 --> 09:02.104
I told you, it wasn't him.

176
09:02.188 --> 09:03.105
Take him!

177
09:04.523 --> 09:06.275
It's suspicious that he ran.

178
09:06.359 --> 09:08.027
Why would he run if he was innocent?

179
09:08.110 --> 09:10.404
The Japanese police were chasing me with guns.

180
09:10.488 --> 09:12.198
Any Joseon person would be scared!

181
09:12.281 --> 09:13.407
Shut up!

182
09:13.491 --> 09:14.992
Wait!

183
09:19.330 --> 09:20.706
-Go! -Yes, sir!

184
09:24.460 --> 09:25.586
You can go on.

185
09:26.545 --> 09:28.339
I'll hold him here.

186
09:28.422 --> 09:30.424
Then I'll leave him in your hands.

187
09:40.726 --> 09:41.686
Go on, now.

188
09:41.769 --> 09:43.854
Are you from Joseon?

189
09:44.605 --> 09:45.439
I'm…

190
09:51.028 --> 09:52.363
Just go.

191
09:52.446 --> 09:53.531
Thank you.

192
09:55.491 --> 09:56.492
Thank you.

193
10:11.882 --> 10:14.301
THE FIRST JONGNO PAWNSHOP

194
10:14.385 --> 10:15.386
Seriously?

195
10:16.721 --> 10:18.514
It really says "The First."

196
10:26.939 --> 10:27.773
Let's go.

197
10:29.650 --> 10:30.943
Hold on.

198
10:32.486 --> 10:33.529
What's going on?

199
10:34.196 --> 10:36.449
Where's the person who wore this?

200
10:38.200 --> 10:39.076
Well…

201
10:40.202 --> 10:41.704
Apparently, some man reported

202
10:41.787 --> 10:44.248
that his wife was cheating on him in this inn.

203
10:44.331 --> 10:46.500
So the police came to catch them red-handed.

204
10:46.584 --> 10:49.545
It's absolute chaos. That man is waiting outside.

205
10:49.628 --> 10:50.588
So…

206
10:51.172 --> 10:53.048
did you see what he looked like?

207
10:53.132 --> 10:55.050
He had these red eyes.

208
10:55.593 --> 10:59.346
Right, he was asking if anyone had seen a woman with a red-jeweled ring.

209
10:59.430 --> 11:00.848
Is she here?

210
11:00.931 --> 11:01.807
Oh my.

211
11:02.808 --> 11:06.395
Is there something I can help you with?

212
11:08.564 --> 11:10.691
She said if we traded clothes,

213
11:10.775 --> 11:13.778
my husband would follow her instead.

214
11:15.112 --> 11:16.071
What?

215
11:36.300 --> 11:38.385
Let's not see each other again.

216
11:41.055 --> 11:43.098
Wait. It fits perfectly.

217
11:43.849 --> 11:45.935
Should I keep this instead of selling it?

218
12:09.166 --> 12:14.296
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

219
12:15.381 --> 12:17.091
Do you mean that customer from earlier?

220
12:18.175 --> 12:22.179
How would I know where all my customers live?

221
12:22.263 --> 12:23.556
I'm very sorry.

222
12:24.640 --> 12:25.850
Yes, I understand.

223
12:26.767 --> 12:28.269
All right. Go on already.

224
12:28.853 --> 12:31.397
You said you didn't know anything about Jongno Pawnshop.

225
12:32.147 --> 12:33.315
Do you happen to know

226
12:33.399 --> 12:35.401
a person named Sin Tae-jin?

227
12:35.484 --> 12:36.902
Sin Tae-jin?

228
12:36.986 --> 12:38.279
Sin Tae-jin…

229
12:38.362 --> 12:40.322
Sin Tae-jin…

230
12:40.906 --> 12:42.700
I've never heard that name before.

231
12:42.783 --> 12:44.493
Who could that be?

232
12:45.369 --> 12:47.496
Never mind. You have a good day.

233
12:47.997 --> 12:50.040
All right. You should really get going.

234
12:50.124 --> 12:53.544
APPRAISAL

235
12:56.839 --> 12:58.591
That shaved years off my life.

236
12:58.674 --> 13:00.134
JONGNO PAWNSHOP MAIN BRANCH

237
13:00.217 --> 13:01.218
JONGNO PAWNSHOP BRANCH 2

238
13:02.720 --> 13:04.263
JUNGRO PAWNSHOP

239
13:05.556 --> 13:07.224
ORIGINAL JONGNO PAWNSHOP

240
13:08.017 --> 13:09.435
NEW JONGNO PAWNSHOP

241
13:09.518 --> 13:11.061
JONGRU PAWNSHOP

242
13:11.145 --> 13:12.563
JEONGRO PAWNSHOP

243
13:12.646 --> 13:14.273
REAL JONGNO PAWNSHOP

244
13:16.358 --> 13:19.653
So it wasn't a lie.

245
13:19.737 --> 13:21.739
JONGNO PAWNSHOP

246
14:06.867 --> 14:08.160
Mother.

247
14:26.971 --> 14:28.305
Who are you?

248
14:30.432 --> 14:33.560
I'm Sato Hideo, Mr. Suzuki's colleague at the Government-General.

249
14:34.144 --> 14:35.604
Oh, I see.

250
14:37.523 --> 14:40.067
He has no family.

251
14:40.150 --> 14:42.152
If anything happens, please contact me.

252
14:43.278 --> 14:44.446
Please take good care of him.

253
14:45.781 --> 14:46.657
I will.

254
14:51.912 --> 14:54.373
It's a great honor to serve you again

255
14:54.456 --> 14:57.418
as chief of police of the Government-General of Joseon, sir.

256
14:59.044 --> 15:02.006
You left for Japan in 1920, didn't you?

257
15:02.798 --> 15:04.091
I did.

258
15:04.842 --> 15:06.260
How have you been?

259
15:06.343 --> 15:08.345
Very well, thanks to you.

260
15:10.305 --> 15:14.643
Compared to how I was starving before I came to Joseon back in 1912,

261
15:15.310 --> 15:16.895
Keijo feels like paradise.

262
15:19.231 --> 15:21.066
Back in 1912…

263
15:21.817 --> 15:24.111
You've been in Joseon for 20 years now.

264
15:24.653 --> 15:25.571
Yes.

265
15:25.654 --> 15:27.573
Do you remember what you told me

266
15:28.532 --> 15:31.118
when we first met that year?

267
15:32.786 --> 15:35.956
"Three years for a stone. Give Joseon ten."

268
15:36.040 --> 15:38.459
"As the old saying goes, even a cold stone warms up

269
15:38.542 --> 15:39.918
if you sit on it for three years."

270
15:40.627 --> 15:43.213
"Even if life is hard in this foreign land,

271
15:43.297 --> 15:44.506
it's still better

272
15:45.174 --> 15:48.469
than being treated like dirt and starving in Japan. Just hold out for ten years."

273
15:49.720 --> 15:51.680
You told me to keep that in mind.

274
15:53.474 --> 15:56.268
I've kept those words close to my heart and made it this far.

275
15:56.351 --> 15:57.770
I see.

276
15:58.687 --> 16:00.814
For people like you and me,

277
16:01.815 --> 16:03.484
Joseon is still

278
16:03.567 --> 16:06.320
a land of opportunity, now and for years to come.

279
16:07.654 --> 16:09.031
-Fukuda. -Sir.

280
16:09.990 --> 16:12.409
After 20 years in Joseon,

281
16:13.243 --> 16:14.661
is chief of police all you want?

282
16:16.371 --> 16:17.331
Pardon?

283
16:26.715 --> 16:28.258
You have my absolute loyalty!

284
16:28.926 --> 16:30.469
Prove your loyalty

285
16:31.220 --> 16:33.347
by wiping out the Gugukdan.

286
16:33.931 --> 16:34.848
Yes, sir!

287
16:46.693 --> 16:50.364
I hardly had any customers, so I didn't run around much.

288
16:50.447 --> 16:54.034
But why do my rubber shoes keep wearing out?

289
16:54.785 --> 16:56.787
Did you barely have any customers today?

290
16:57.412 --> 16:58.539
No.

291
16:58.622 --> 17:02.584
There are so many taxis these days, I can barely get one passenger a day.

292
17:02.668 --> 17:05.337
They call it the age of speed or whatever.

293
17:05.420 --> 17:07.506
I managed to get one passenger today,

294
17:07.589 --> 17:08.757
and he was a traitor.

295
17:09.967 --> 17:12.052
Some Joseon scum working at the Government-General.

296
17:12.719 --> 17:14.138
A Joseon man at the Government-General?

297
17:14.221 --> 17:16.640
Not a Joseon man. He's Joseon scum.

298
17:16.723 --> 17:19.268
How could a Joseon person possibly work at the Government-General?

299
17:20.686 --> 17:21.687
Good grief.

300
17:21.770 --> 17:22.813
My back hurts.

301
17:23.397 --> 17:24.523
Hey, No-ma.

302
17:24.606 --> 17:27.943
Why don't you try delivering food instead of pulling a rickshaw?

303
17:28.026 --> 17:29.945
-A delivery boy? -Yeah.

304
17:30.028 --> 17:31.071
On a bicycle?

305
17:31.155 --> 17:33.407
These days, more and more people are having things

306
17:33.490 --> 17:35.242
like seolleongtang and naengmyeon delivered.

307
17:36.326 --> 17:38.996
Do you think I can get whatever I want?

308
17:39.079 --> 17:41.165
Bicycles don't come cheap, you know.

309
17:41.748 --> 17:44.418
What else can you do? You said there are no customers.

310
17:49.214 --> 17:50.132
Are you asleep?

311
17:55.345 --> 17:57.556
He hasn't made a penny, yet he's fast asleep.

312
18:27.252 --> 18:29.963
I almost went to prison before I made it to America.

313
18:39.514 --> 18:41.600
What could he have left at the pawnshop?

314
18:42.935 --> 18:43.810
Hold on.

315
18:44.311 --> 18:47.272
Sin Tae-jin is a Joseon name.

316
18:49.608 --> 18:50.651
Unbelievable.

317
18:50.734 --> 18:53.987
As if taking our country wasn't enough, they even stole our pawn tickets!

318
18:56.782 --> 18:57.616
Seriously…

319
19:00.452 --> 19:02.537
BOUNTY 300 WON

320
19:03.372 --> 19:05.958
BOUNTY 500 WON

321
19:08.126 --> 19:11.380
HANSEONG MEDICINE CLINIC

322
19:11.463 --> 19:13.757
SUSPECT'S DESCRIPTION NAME: HAN CHEOL-YONG

323
19:15.759 --> 19:17.094
Please take this.

324
19:17.177 --> 19:19.513
You should be able to lie low for a while.

325
19:20.264 --> 19:21.556
Oh dear.

326
19:21.640 --> 19:22.933
I'm grateful,

327
19:23.016 --> 19:25.102
but I hate to impose on you like this.

328
19:25.185 --> 19:26.270
You know who I am.

329
19:26.853 --> 19:29.690
I'm the only daughter of Joil Textile Factory's president,

330
19:29.773 --> 19:31.441
Joseon's biggest traitor, and a marquess.

331
19:36.196 --> 19:38.782
I'm ashamed that I can't punish my father myself.

332
19:39.366 --> 19:41.243
So I want to make amends this way.

333
19:41.326 --> 19:42.160
Thank you.

334
19:43.412 --> 19:44.997
Lee Young-bok, my father's secretary,

335
19:45.080 --> 19:47.165
managed to siphon off company funds.

336
19:48.208 --> 19:51.420
In an emergency, it's quicker than selling my gold jewelry.

337
19:53.797 --> 19:54.881
How is Suzuki doing?

338
19:54.965 --> 19:57.926
The worst has passed, but he's not out of the woods yet.

339
19:58.802 --> 20:01.555
Sato Hideo came to visit Suzuki a few days ago.

340
20:02.639 --> 20:04.933
He told me to take good care of Suzuki

341
20:05.017 --> 20:06.476
since he has no family to turn to.

342
20:07.352 --> 20:09.438
As if he cares about his colleague.

343
20:10.022 --> 20:12.024
He's Sato Shinichi's son.

344
20:12.107 --> 20:14.234
He'd shoot us without a second thought.

345
20:14.818 --> 20:18.363
He's right. He did a fine job protecting his father that day too.

346
20:18.947 --> 20:20.991
Then who shot Sato that day?

347
20:22.242 --> 20:25.370
Why did the Government-General start coming after us over that?

348
20:25.454 --> 20:29.166
If we'd killed Sato, I'd understand. But this feels a little unfair.

349
20:30.834 --> 20:34.338
Without Suzuki, no one can tell us what's going on at the Government-General,

350
20:34.421 --> 20:36.673
let alone Sato's schedule and movements.

351
20:38.342 --> 20:40.385
PERSONNEL NOTICE GOVERNMENT-GENERAL INTERPRETER

352
20:44.514 --> 20:49.061
The interpreter trainee spot at the Government-General is open.

353
20:49.895 --> 20:53.607
Sato Hideo, the interpreter trainee, was moved into Suzuki's position,

354
20:53.690 --> 20:56.151
leaving the interpreter trainee's post vacant.

355
20:56.234 --> 20:57.110
Are you saying

356
20:57.986 --> 21:00.989
you want to put another spy in that interpreter trainee post?

357
21:01.073 --> 21:01.948
Yes.

358
21:02.783 --> 21:05.035
We need one of our people in the Government-General.

359
21:05.619 --> 21:06.953
We all know that.

360
21:07.037 --> 21:08.830
But how do we get someone in there?

361
21:08.914 --> 21:10.874
An interpreter trainee has to speak English.

362
21:10.957 --> 21:13.126
It's hard to find fluent English speakers.

363
21:13.210 --> 21:14.336
Is there anyone like that?

364
21:15.379 --> 21:16.505
There is.

365
21:17.130 --> 21:18.298
Who is that?

366
21:20.133 --> 21:22.636
The girl who posed as a live-in maid at our house.

367
21:23.220 --> 21:24.721
What? A live-in maid?

368
21:24.805 --> 21:27.265
She's sharp and a good liar.

369
21:27.349 --> 21:29.017
She's quick on her feet.

370
21:29.101 --> 21:30.435
She had the nerve to come

371
21:30.519 --> 21:32.938
while we were hosting Sato and pressure us.

372
21:33.021 --> 21:37.359
And she's quick with her hands, and her English is surprisingly good.

373
21:40.946 --> 21:41.780
Right.

374
21:41.863 --> 21:44.032
I've verified her English skills.

375
21:44.116 --> 21:46.952
But I'm against sending her in as a spy.

376
21:47.035 --> 21:48.662
A spy holds not only our lives

377
21:49.538 --> 21:51.790
but the fate of the Shanghai headquarters in their hands.

378
21:53.125 --> 21:54.126
We can't put someone

379
21:54.209 --> 21:56.586
who doesn't care about independence in that position.

380
21:57.295 --> 21:59.589
I'm worried that we just let her go.

381
21:59.673 --> 22:00.757
Right.

382
22:01.258 --> 22:04.678
From what I've heard, she seems to care about nothing but money.

383
22:04.761 --> 22:08.098
If we send her as a spy, she could be turned against us with money.

384
22:08.181 --> 22:10.142
She doesn't care about independence,

385
22:10.225 --> 22:11.810
so money will sway her either way.

386
22:12.394 --> 22:13.478
Exactly.

387
22:14.479 --> 22:16.565
She'll work for whoever offers her money.

388
22:17.232 --> 22:20.735
But there's something she wants more than money.

389
22:21.862 --> 22:22.821
She wants…

390
22:23.697 --> 22:24.948
to go to America.

391
22:25.907 --> 22:27.826
What? America?

392
22:27.909 --> 22:31.538
For her, money is just a means to get to America.

393
22:32.038 --> 22:34.374
So if going to America is part of the deal,

394
22:34.458 --> 22:36.793
she won't turn down our offer

395
22:37.461 --> 22:39.129
or betray us.

396
22:40.464 --> 22:42.466
Why does she want to go to America?

397
22:45.051 --> 22:46.720
Don't you care about your own country?

398
22:46.803 --> 22:50.807
Look, I was born into a country already under Japanese rule.

399
22:50.891 --> 22:52.601
Is that my fault?

400
22:52.684 --> 22:54.561
You can't blame me, can you?

401
22:54.644 --> 22:57.230
Am I supposed to fight for independence just because I was born in Joseon?

402
22:59.399 --> 23:01.902
What has Joseon ever done for me?

403
23:04.905 --> 23:06.823
I don't know her story.

404
23:07.407 --> 23:10.118
But her drive to leave Joseon

405
23:10.202 --> 23:13.663
was as strong as our longing for independence.

406
23:14.289 --> 23:18.251
I felt that, deep down, what drove her was hatred.

407
23:19.794 --> 23:23.423
And hatred can be just as powerful as love.

408
23:24.341 --> 23:25.383
Even so,

409
23:25.967 --> 23:28.428
you don't even know her name or where she lives.

410
23:29.346 --> 23:30.972
I may not know where she lives,

411
23:31.932 --> 23:33.975
but I know where to find her.

412
23:44.277 --> 23:45.695
I don't see her anywhere.

413
23:46.446 --> 23:47.948
Oh my!

414
23:50.492 --> 23:51.576
-Are you okay? -Sorry.

415
23:51.660 --> 23:52.827
I'm sorry.

416
23:52.911 --> 23:53.954
Good grief.

417
23:54.746 --> 23:55.705
Thank you.

418
24:06.800 --> 24:07.717
My pocket watch.

419
24:08.969 --> 24:10.929
Goodness, my wallet's gone too.

420
24:14.599 --> 24:15.600
FIRST-CLASS COMPARTMENT

421
24:44.588 --> 24:47.674
"Dear Ms. Hong Gil-sun, I hope you're well."

422
24:47.757 --> 24:51.553
"I'm Lee Yang-buk, Joil Textile Factory president's secretary."

423
24:52.470 --> 24:53.638
Joil Textile Factory?

424
24:54.264 --> 24:55.890
Oh, that Joil Textile Factory.

425
24:56.558 --> 25:00.729
"We extend our sincere thanks to you

426
25:00.812 --> 25:04.774
for applying to serve as our young lady's study companion

427
25:04.858 --> 25:07.068
during her studies in America."

428
25:08.153 --> 25:09.070
America?

429
25:09.613 --> 25:13.450
"There will be an interview at our president's house

430
25:13.533 --> 25:18.872
at 1:00 p.m. on Saturday, April 9th."

431
25:18.955 --> 25:23.835
"If selected, we'll cover all tuition and living expenses

432
25:23.918 --> 25:25.545
for two years of study in America."

433
25:26.379 --> 25:27.255
What?

434
25:28.381 --> 25:29.257
Hang on.

435
25:30.008 --> 25:32.510
"A study companion during her studies in America."

436
25:35.639 --> 25:37.474
Oh my goodness.

437
25:39.225 --> 25:40.352
What's the date today?

438
25:41.645 --> 25:42.562
April 8th.

439
25:43.063 --> 25:44.230
The interview is tomorrow.

440
25:46.941 --> 25:48.526
I can't believe this.

441
25:48.610 --> 25:50.320
Hey, No-ma!

442
25:50.403 --> 25:51.279
No-ma!

443
25:51.363 --> 25:52.989
-One moment. -What's going on?

444
25:53.073 --> 25:54.616
Kkot-nim, we'll be right back.

445
25:54.699 --> 25:55.659
Be right back.

446
25:55.742 --> 25:56.785
Where are you going?

447
25:56.868 --> 25:57.869
It won't take long.

448
26:06.461 --> 26:08.838
It's hard to tell, but have you seen anyone like this?

449
26:08.922 --> 26:10.757
-Nope. -Bad drawing, isn't it?

450
26:10.840 --> 26:12.509
Someone must've drawn it blindfolded.

451
26:15.095 --> 26:16.763
Have you had a female customer like this?

452
26:16.846 --> 26:18.556
-She wears glasses. -No idea.

453
26:18.640 --> 26:20.266
How could anyone tell from that?

454
26:20.350 --> 26:22.477
-Look carefully. -Go away.

455
26:22.560 --> 26:23.478
Wait…

456
26:23.978 --> 26:25.855
Mister.

457
26:25.939 --> 26:29.109
Look, have you ever had a female customer who looks like this?

458
26:29.192 --> 26:30.944
She's from Busan and has an accent.

459
26:33.113 --> 26:33.947
Glasses.

460
26:34.030 --> 26:35.615
Yes, exactly. Glasses.

461
26:35.699 --> 26:37.575
Glasses, right?

462
26:39.244 --> 26:40.203
Do I know you?

463
26:42.455 --> 26:44.207
Are you Ms. Hong Gil-sun?

464
26:44.290 --> 26:46.376
Yes, but who are you?

465
26:46.459 --> 26:49.713
I was sent on an errand for the president of Joil Textile Factory.

466
26:50.505 --> 26:52.799
The Joil Textile Factory president?

467
26:52.882 --> 26:53.967
What brings you here?

468
26:54.843 --> 26:59.305
He sent me to inform you that today's interview has been canceled.

469
27:00.056 --> 27:02.559
What? Canceled?

470
27:02.642 --> 27:03.476
Why?

471
27:03.560 --> 27:06.187
He's decided to go with another candidate.

472
27:06.813 --> 27:09.274
He said he was deeply sorry for the inconvenience

473
27:09.357 --> 27:11.151
and asked me to give you this.

474
27:11.234 --> 27:12.527
What is it?

475
27:13.111 --> 27:15.155
You came all the way from Busan for nothing.

476
27:15.238 --> 27:18.324
He told me to give you this to cover your train fare

477
27:18.408 --> 27:20.243
as a token of his apology.

478
27:24.330 --> 27:25.206
Twenty won.

479
27:25.290 --> 27:27.250
That's a department store clerk's monthly salary.

480
27:27.333 --> 27:28.543
I'm so sorry.

481
27:28.626 --> 27:29.753
It's no small amount.

482
27:30.628 --> 27:32.005
She understands that

483
27:32.088 --> 27:35.383
sometimes she has to give something first to get what she wants.

484
27:41.139 --> 27:42.140
Oh my.

485
27:45.185 --> 27:47.562
Please wait here for a moment, Ms. Hong.

486
27:48.354 --> 27:49.355
Sure.

487
27:49.981 --> 27:50.899
Thanks.

488
27:53.067 --> 27:54.110
Young lady?

489
27:55.987 --> 27:57.739
She looks so gorgeous.

490
27:58.615 --> 28:02.035
She looks like actress Kim Yeon-sil, doesn't she?

491
28:03.828 --> 28:06.915
No, she's prettier than Kim Yeon-sil.

492
28:06.998 --> 28:08.208
Right?

493
28:08.833 --> 28:10.335
Then I'll go bring her.

494
28:11.336 --> 28:12.337
Okay.

495
28:15.632 --> 28:17.383
What's his problem? She's pretty.

496
28:48.331 --> 28:50.625
I should make a good impression, so I'll just look.

497
28:51.292 --> 28:53.211
Don't be penny-wise and pound-foolish.

498
29:01.719 --> 29:04.430
Hello, I'm Hong Gil-sun…

499
29:18.361 --> 29:19.612
So you're saying

500
29:20.154 --> 29:24.450
you set the whole thing up, and I played right into your hands?

501
29:25.285 --> 29:27.287
If that's how you want to put it,

502
29:27.370 --> 29:28.329
then yes.

503
29:31.374 --> 29:33.918
You said your business fell through because of me last time.

504
29:34.002 --> 29:35.003
We're even now, right?

505
29:36.421 --> 29:38.756
I hope we never see each other again.

506
29:40.341 --> 29:43.219
What about my 20 won? Did I just lose that?

507
29:49.058 --> 29:50.101
I'll send you to America.

508
29:51.853 --> 29:52.687
What?

509
29:53.271 --> 29:55.148
You said you wanted to go to America.

510
29:56.024 --> 29:57.317
In return, work with us.

511
29:58.610 --> 30:00.194
Work at the Government-General.

512
30:02.030 --> 30:03.197
The Government-General?

513
30:05.909 --> 30:06.993
You can't be serious.

514
30:07.577 --> 30:09.078
Are you saying

515
30:09.913 --> 30:11.623
you want me to be a spy?

516
30:11.706 --> 30:12.707
Yes.

517
30:13.416 --> 30:16.336
Infiltrate the Government-General as a spy and work for us.

518
30:17.420 --> 30:21.257
The Japanese keep infiltrating our government and independence groups.

519
30:21.341 --> 30:24.052
The Japanese aren't the only ones who can plant spies.

520
30:25.178 --> 30:27.680
Look, I'm not an idiot.

521
30:27.764 --> 30:30.099
I ended up falling for the promise of America today,

522
30:30.183 --> 30:33.227
but I'm usually the one who tricks others, not the other way around.

523
30:33.311 --> 30:36.022
You enjoyed messing with me today, so why keep pushing?

524
30:37.482 --> 30:40.693
Even for a thousand won, I'm not doing it.

525
30:40.777 --> 30:43.279
I don't want to get involved in the independence movement.

526
30:43.363 --> 30:45.323
I don't want to die before I make it to America.

527
30:45.406 --> 30:48.910
I believe I told you the other day. You can't go to America now.

528
30:48.993 --> 30:51.663
You keep telling me I can't go there.

529
30:51.746 --> 30:54.165
Is it fun to mess with someone's desperate hopes?

530
30:54.248 --> 30:56.793
I'm talking about the current situation in America.

531
30:57.710 --> 31:00.421
For years now, America has banned immigration from Asia

532
31:00.505 --> 31:01.839
based on the Immigration Act.

533
31:01.923 --> 31:03.341
Don't be ridiculous.

534
31:03.424 --> 31:04.884
I've never heard of such a thing.

535
31:06.177 --> 31:08.972
Just because you don't know doesn't mean it doesn't exist.

536
31:09.055 --> 31:12.266
But we'll send you to America

537
31:12.767 --> 31:14.560
as long as you accept our offer.

538
31:14.644 --> 31:15.853
Excuse me.

539
31:15.937 --> 31:18.231
You're contradicting yourself.

540
31:18.314 --> 31:21.901
You just said American law won't allow me to go to America.

541
31:21.985 --> 31:25.279
Then how exactly are you going to get me there?

542
31:25.363 --> 31:26.572
Did you forget?

543
31:27.448 --> 31:30.159
My husband is American, and he's a journalist.

544
31:30.243 --> 31:32.161
It means he's not an ordinary Joseon man.

545
31:32.745 --> 31:34.706
Whatever. I'm out of here.

546
31:36.541 --> 31:39.752
Don't ever think about trying to hurt me.

547
31:39.836 --> 31:41.254
If I'm not home by tonight,

548
31:41.337 --> 31:45.258
they'll take the bullets and the suitcase to Jongno Police Station and report them.

549
31:45.341 --> 31:48.302
Do you think the police will believe you?

550
31:48.386 --> 31:50.388
You're with the Gugukdan, aren't you?

551
31:51.389 --> 31:53.016
You'd better let me go quietly--

552
31:53.099 --> 31:54.100
Lee Ga-kyung.

553
31:56.644 --> 31:58.813
Who is that?

554
32:00.314 --> 32:01.190
Lee Ga-kyung?

555
32:01.274 --> 32:04.694
As an orphan, you worked as a live-in maid for an American missionary.

556
32:04.777 --> 32:08.197
You've been living in the shantytown in Gyodang-ri these past few years.

557
32:09.073 --> 32:10.783
You live with a young rickshaw puller

558
32:10.867 --> 32:12.827
and a little girl who can't walk.

559
32:12.910 --> 32:15.371
They're not your husband and daughter.

560
32:15.455 --> 32:16.956
Lee No-ma and Bang Kkot-nim?

561
32:17.832 --> 32:19.500
I don't know what you're talking about.

562
32:19.584 --> 32:22.170
You told those two to report it, didn't you?

563
32:22.253 --> 32:25.214
But who do you think those two are with now?

564
32:25.298 --> 32:28.760
I really have no idea what you're talking about.

565
32:29.469 --> 32:30.511
Fine.

566
32:32.805 --> 32:34.098
Let me ask you something.

567
32:34.182 --> 32:37.185
You're smart, resourceful, and even fluent in English.

568
32:37.268 --> 32:38.603
Why do you live like this?

569
32:38.686 --> 32:40.897
That's none of your business.

570
32:41.731 --> 32:44.233
Then why do you live like this?

571
32:44.317 --> 32:46.486
Why do you fight for independence?

572
32:46.569 --> 32:48.154
You could die doing that.

573
32:48.237 --> 32:50.531
I might as well have died a long time ago.

574
32:50.615 --> 32:51.991
So I'm not afraid of death.

575
32:56.621 --> 32:58.664
Someday, I hope you'll make it

576
32:59.373 --> 33:01.584
to America, Ga-kyung.

577
33:02.919 --> 33:04.045
Go there

578
33:04.629 --> 33:06.172
and be happy.

579
33:07.840 --> 33:10.093
I told you, I'm not Lee Ga-kyung.

580
33:19.769 --> 33:20.686
But you know what?

581
33:21.938 --> 33:25.233
If you plan to die fighting for independence, don't have children.

582
33:26.234 --> 33:27.527
Whatever the reason,

583
33:27.610 --> 33:30.238
there's nothing worse than leaving a child all alone.

584
33:47.296 --> 33:51.300
Why did you just let her go when she rejected the offer?

585
34:01.352 --> 34:02.770
That's what I'm wondering.

586
34:03.855 --> 34:05.731
Who says I can't go to America?

587
34:06.315 --> 34:07.191
Unbelievable.

588
34:08.192 --> 34:11.279
I'll go to America just fine on my own. Spare me your concern!

589
34:23.124 --> 34:26.127
I really can't go to America even if I save up enough money?

590
34:27.253 --> 34:28.087
Why not?

591
34:30.089 --> 34:31.007
Damn it.

592
34:32.341 --> 34:34.010
She wasn't lying.

593
34:37.555 --> 34:38.890
Lee No-ma, Bang Kkot…

594
34:39.390 --> 34:40.433
Kkot-nim!

595
34:40.516 --> 34:42.059
Lee No-ma!

596
34:42.143 --> 34:43.227
Bang Kkot-nim!

597
34:50.026 --> 34:50.860
Thank goodness.

598
34:51.444 --> 34:52.445
They're all right.

599
34:56.908 --> 34:59.619
What the hell? And now this one's a lie?

600
35:01.996 --> 35:02.914
I'm exhausted.

601
35:03.623 --> 35:04.457
Kkot-nim.

602
35:08.544 --> 35:09.378
Bang Kkot-nim.

603
35:10.796 --> 35:13.633
Why are you crying?

604
35:14.759 --> 35:16.219
Why are you crying, Kkot-nim?

605
35:16.886 --> 35:18.137
Did the kids pick on you again?

606
35:19.430 --> 35:20.264
Hey.

607
35:21.140 --> 35:21.974
You…

608
35:23.226 --> 35:24.602
What happened to your face?

609
35:25.770 --> 35:26.604
Why…

610
35:35.279 --> 35:36.113
You're here?

611
35:45.623 --> 35:46.958
What are you doing?

612
35:47.875 --> 35:49.043
What do you think?

613
35:49.126 --> 35:51.504
I'm checking out the little stash

614
35:51.587 --> 35:56.133
my pretty Ga-kyung has been hiding under my roof.

615
35:57.760 --> 35:59.553
Wow, how much is all this?

616
35:59.637 --> 36:03.015
One won, five won… This is impressive.

617
36:03.099 --> 36:04.850
It's not a secret stash. It's my daily wages.

618
36:04.934 --> 36:06.102
Give it back.

619
36:06.727 --> 36:07.770
Daily wages?

620
36:08.396 --> 36:10.231
You pretty little bitch.

621
36:10.773 --> 36:13.901
You're quite the liar, aren't you?

622
36:14.568 --> 36:16.487
Don't take that. It's my money.

623
36:16.570 --> 36:17.947
Give back my money!

624
36:19.615 --> 36:20.616
Your money?

625
36:21.325 --> 36:22.159
Your money?

626
36:23.577 --> 36:25.121
What money here is yours?

627
36:25.204 --> 36:29.125
Who do you think lets you make a living picking other people's pockets?

628
36:29.792 --> 36:30.668
Ga-kyung!

629
36:30.751 --> 36:33.254
And you still owe me, remember?

630
36:33.337 --> 36:34.714
Don't hit her. Just talk to her.

631
36:34.797 --> 36:37.049
-Let go already! -She really saved it from her wages.

632
36:37.633 --> 36:38.634
Get the hell off me!

633
36:41.053 --> 36:41.929
Answer me.

634
36:42.555 --> 36:43.472
I said answer me.

635
36:43.556 --> 36:46.642
Whose turf is Gyeongseong Station?

636
36:46.726 --> 36:48.686
Who's the one bribing the police

637
36:48.769 --> 36:51.564
to look the other way when you pickpocket?

638
36:51.647 --> 36:53.316
Whose house do you think this is?

639
36:53.399 --> 36:55.526
If I hadn't taken you in back then,

640
36:55.609 --> 36:58.446
that Sinjeong Red-Light District would be your home now.

641
36:59.071 --> 36:59.905
Do you know that?

642
37:00.656 --> 37:01.782
After all I've done for you,

643
37:01.866 --> 37:04.118
you stole my money and tried to sneak out of the country.

644
37:04.827 --> 37:08.122
I let you off once, and now you're stashing money behind my back?

645
37:08.706 --> 37:10.583
That's enough, Boss. Please stop.

646
37:13.377 --> 37:15.087
You're in on this together, aren't you?

647
37:15.755 --> 37:18.049
When you asked me to let this bitch stay here,

648
37:18.132 --> 37:19.008
what did I say?

649
37:19.091 --> 37:21.886
I warned you not to stab me in the back over some bitch.

650
37:21.969 --> 37:23.596
Did I or didn't I?

651
37:25.181 --> 37:26.349
It's not like that!

652
37:26.432 --> 37:27.558
Don't hit him!

653
37:34.732 --> 37:35.941
You damn bitch!

654
37:37.943 --> 37:41.155
You said if I caught you hiding money from me,

655
37:41.238 --> 37:43.240
you'd pay me back with your body.

656
37:45.076 --> 37:46.660
Today is the day.

657
37:48.829 --> 37:49.663
Get over here.

658
37:51.624 --> 37:52.541
Come here.

659
37:54.919 --> 37:56.087
Hold still.

660
38:00.758 --> 38:03.302
Stop, Boss. I'll give you all the money.

661
38:03.386 --> 38:05.262
Leave Ga-kyung alone.

662
38:07.848 --> 38:09.141
For goodness' sake!

663
38:09.225 --> 38:10.726
Do you really want to die? Damn it.

664
38:10.810 --> 38:11.894
Back off.

665
38:12.937 --> 38:14.063
Don't.

666
38:14.146 --> 38:15.314
Stop, Boss.

667
38:15.398 --> 38:17.108
-Let go. -Boss.

668
38:17.900 --> 38:20.194
I said let go! Let go!

669
38:22.571 --> 38:24.073
You bastard.

670
38:24.156 --> 38:25.991
Sorry. Please stop.

671
38:27.284 --> 38:29.245
-Let go! -Boss.

672
38:29.328 --> 38:31.414
-I said just let go of me! -Boss.

673
38:34.625 --> 38:37.336
I'm sorry, please forgive me.

674
38:40.214 --> 38:41.757
Get off me!

675
38:46.345 --> 38:48.556
Lee No-ma, you idiot.

676
38:48.639 --> 38:50.099
Snap out of it.

677
38:50.182 --> 38:52.268
Do you know what kind of bitch she is?

678
38:52.351 --> 38:54.520
Apparently, her mom

679
38:55.020 --> 38:56.939
went screwing around with a Jap.

680
38:58.315 --> 38:59.692
She was a gisaeng

681
39:00.651 --> 39:02.111
who shacked up with a Jap.

682
39:05.656 --> 39:08.117
When your mom and dad

683
39:08.200 --> 39:12.288
were getting shot dead in the head shouting, "Independence for Korea,"

684
39:12.371 --> 39:15.291
her mom was sleeping with a Jap.

685
39:15.374 --> 39:16.834
You didn't know, did you?

686
39:18.043 --> 39:18.878
No.

687
39:19.837 --> 39:21.005
That's not true, right?

688
39:21.547 --> 39:25.634
Ga-kyung's mother died of tuberculosis when she was little.

689
39:25.718 --> 39:26.760
Tuberculosis?

690
39:30.598 --> 39:31.849
Tuberculosis.

691
39:34.268 --> 39:35.853
Lee Ga-kyung, seriously,

692
39:35.936 --> 39:39.982
you're one hell of a liar. I have to hand it to you.

693
39:40.649 --> 39:44.028
How could you hide that from No-ma, of all people?

694
39:44.111 --> 39:46.030
Were you afraid

695
39:46.113 --> 39:48.073
he would throw you out if he found out?

696
39:48.866 --> 39:49.700
Hey.

697
39:50.284 --> 39:51.577
Do you know why

698
39:51.660 --> 39:53.579
that bitch's so good at pickpocketing?

699
39:55.122 --> 39:56.790
It's in her blood.

700
39:57.374 --> 40:00.044
She's got the blood of the Japanese who stole our country.

701
40:00.127 --> 40:03.172
The blood of a thief is bound to show.

702
40:04.340 --> 40:07.635
Hey, do you think your mother hooked up with a Jap just once?

703
40:08.219 --> 40:11.555
You know deep down you've probably got Jap blood in you,

704
40:12.306 --> 40:13.265
don't you?

705
40:16.560 --> 40:17.645
You pitiful wench.

706
40:19.939 --> 40:21.357
Watch your mouth.

707
40:21.440 --> 40:22.358
What?

708
40:22.441 --> 40:24.193
She's still your mother,

709
40:24.276 --> 40:25.903
so you're upset because I insulted her?

710
40:25.986 --> 40:27.154
No!

711
40:28.948 --> 40:31.033
Watch your mouth about me.

712
40:31.575 --> 40:32.409
What?

713
40:33.953 --> 40:34.787
I am…

714
40:36.580 --> 40:38.165
not pitiful.

715
40:39.416 --> 40:40.376
What are you, then?

716
40:42.795 --> 40:44.922
If you're not pitiful,

717
40:46.090 --> 40:47.299
then what are you?

718
41:04.233 --> 41:06.193
-Did you see her face? -I did.

719
41:10.197 --> 41:11.532
You disgust me.

720
41:11.615 --> 41:12.950
That filthy blood!

721
41:13.033 --> 41:14.451
Get out of my house!

722
41:27.298 --> 41:31.010
Why are you hitting it so hard? Are you mad at your husband?

723
41:31.510 --> 41:33.178
Oh, I am.

724
41:33.971 --> 41:36.307
I haven't seen the widow from the shop lately.

725
41:36.390 --> 41:39.310
She had an affair with a Japanese man and ran off to Japan.

726
41:39.393 --> 41:41.103
No wonder I haven't seen her around.

727
41:45.232 --> 41:46.859
Hey, wait.

728
41:47.443 --> 41:50.070
Aren't you the live-in maid at the American's house?

729
41:51.989 --> 41:53.699
It must be hard.

730
41:54.325 --> 41:55.951
Why don't you work at a textile factory?

731
41:56.035 --> 41:58.704
The factory is nice and warm.

732
42:01.665 --> 42:03.000
Don't come any closer!

733
42:04.793 --> 42:06.128
Why do you keep saying no?

734
42:06.795 --> 42:09.673
Weren't you after a Japanese guy too?

735
42:09.757 --> 42:11.300
Just like your mother?

736
42:47.378 --> 42:48.462
I'll do it.

737
42:50.381 --> 42:52.966
Send me to America, and I'll work for you

738
42:53.592 --> 42:54.426
as your spy.

739
43:21.954 --> 43:23.414
There are conditions, though.

740
43:24.081 --> 43:26.291
I want a bonus on top of my base pay.

741
43:27.000 --> 43:28.168
A bonus?

742
43:28.252 --> 43:31.338
I hear Government-General employees get a bonus on top of their base salary.

743
43:31.422 --> 43:33.215
That's only for Japanese employees.

744
43:33.298 --> 43:34.967
You're a Joseon employee, so you don't get a bonus.

745
43:35.050 --> 43:35.884
Is that so?

746
43:36.593 --> 43:40.055
Then the Gugukdan can pay me the bonus.

747
43:40.139 --> 43:41.473
That's my first condition.

748
43:43.434 --> 43:44.560
What's the second one?

749
43:45.811 --> 43:48.188
Let me eat and sleep here for free.

750
43:50.691 --> 43:52.901
I admit, I'm after money.

751
43:52.985 --> 43:54.194
But living under the same roof

752
43:54.278 --> 43:56.280
won't raise suspicion even if we're together.

753
43:56.864 --> 43:59.199
I'll stay here as a tenant, not a live-in maid.

754
44:00.200 --> 44:02.119
I'll only do this

755
44:02.828 --> 44:04.288
for three months.

756
44:57.925 --> 45:00.636
After three months, send me to America.

757
45:01.386 --> 45:03.472
We have conditions too.

758
45:04.348 --> 45:05.682
First, don't ask any questions.

759
45:06.767 --> 45:09.228
You just do what we tell you.

760
45:10.437 --> 45:11.980
You don't get to ask why.

761
45:12.731 --> 45:13.565
Second,

762
45:14.358 --> 45:16.276
don't steal anything from this house.

763
45:17.528 --> 45:18.654
And finally,

764
45:19.988 --> 45:21.406
don't betray us.

765
45:22.574 --> 45:24.368
There's no mercy for traitors.

766
45:24.451 --> 45:26.453
I was about to say the same thing.

767
45:28.038 --> 45:31.792
Hideo isn't Sato's real son. Sato adopted a Joseon boy.

768
45:32.918 --> 45:33.961
He's from Joseon?

769
45:34.044 --> 45:34.920
That's right.

770
45:35.003 --> 45:37.631
He was an orphan living on the streets in Gyeongseong.

771
45:37.714 --> 45:40.342
He was adopted by Sato when he was about 12.

772
45:42.135 --> 45:44.304
The inspector general comes

773
45:44.388 --> 45:47.432
from a fallen samurai family that came to Joseon in his father's time.

774
45:47.516 --> 45:49.560
To overcome being a colonial resident,

775
45:49.643 --> 45:52.479
he attended the Imperial Japanese Army Academy

776
45:52.563 --> 45:55.315
and returned to Joseon as a soldier.

777
45:56.567 --> 45:58.819
He adopted a Joseon orphan

778
45:58.902 --> 46:01.989
to show how faithfully he supported Japan's policies.

779
46:05.742 --> 46:08.036
His adopted son, Sato Hideo,

780
46:08.120 --> 46:09.538
is a Joseon man only by birth.

781
46:09.621 --> 46:11.874
He also graduated from the Imperial Japanese Army Academy

782
46:11.957 --> 46:13.959
and works for the Government-General of Joseon.

783
46:15.043 --> 46:18.005
He's Japanese through and through.

784
46:18.088 --> 46:21.049
Most importantly, he's the inspector general's son.

785
46:22.342 --> 46:23.927
Keep your guard up around him.

786
46:24.803 --> 46:25.637
Okay.

787
46:26.555 --> 46:27.723
I'll keep that in mind.

788
46:28.473 --> 46:31.184
INTERPRETER SATO HIDEO INTERPRETER TRAINEE KEUM SEO-HEE

789
46:33.478 --> 46:34.563
Good morning.

790
46:36.189 --> 46:40.903
I'm Keum Seo-hee, the new interpreter trainee assigned here.

791
46:40.986 --> 46:43.530
I look forward to working with you.

792
46:44.031 --> 46:46.617
Likewise. I look forward to it.

793
46:48.201 --> 46:50.287
I'll do my best to assist you.

794
46:51.496 --> 46:52.706
Thank you.

795
46:56.376 --> 46:59.212
The League of Nations Commission will come to Gyeongseong soon.

796
47:01.256 --> 47:04.009
The Manchurian Incident, the Shanghai Incident.

797
47:04.968 --> 47:08.096
China claims Japan illegally invaded Manchuria.

798
47:08.180 --> 47:12.142
Japan claims it was exercising its right to self-defense.

799
47:13.602 --> 47:16.146
That's why the League of Nations Commission

800
47:16.229 --> 47:19.441
is going around Manchuria conducting their investigation.

801
47:19.524 --> 47:22.110
They're getting paid to be there, after all.

802
47:23.987 --> 47:26.156
But they're coming here as well.

803
47:26.239 --> 47:27.199
Isn't it obvious?

804
47:27.282 --> 47:29.242
To get a glimpse of Manchuria's future,

805
47:29.326 --> 47:32.496
they can look at Joseon under Japanese rule.

806
47:32.579 --> 47:34.831
We received word that the Commission

807
47:34.915 --> 47:37.584
wants to visit our newspaper while they're in Gyeongseong.

808
47:38.085 --> 47:38.919
Is that so?

809
47:39.503 --> 47:41.797
Yes, and as you know, sir,

810
47:41.880 --> 47:44.549
one of the two Western journalists coming with the Commission

811
47:44.633 --> 47:46.510
is our paper's bureau chief in the Far East.

812
47:48.095 --> 47:48.929
Right.

813
47:50.847 --> 47:54.559
And wouldn't you know it, I'm Joseon-American.

814
47:55.852 --> 47:57.980
If I were to tell the Commission

815
47:58.063 --> 48:00.774
that Japan is doing a fine job developing Joseon,

816
48:02.067 --> 48:03.568
that'd make a useful reference

817
48:03.652 --> 48:05.696
for their report, don't you think?

818
48:05.779 --> 48:08.365
If all goes well, the League of Nations

819
48:08.448 --> 48:11.368
might even recognize Manchukuo as a legitimate independent state.

820
48:13.412 --> 48:15.539
I'll leave it in your hands.

821
48:17.624 --> 48:19.543
Of course. I'll do everything I can.

822
48:20.711 --> 48:22.129
Speaking of which,

823
48:22.212 --> 48:25.799
while they're in Gyeongseong, they'll need interpreters, I'd imagine.

824
48:26.717 --> 48:27.551
Indeed.

825
48:29.511 --> 48:32.180
Yes, the Government-General's Foreign Affairs Division

826
48:32.264 --> 48:34.599
will provide interpretation during their visit.

827
48:35.517 --> 48:36.893
Just as I thought.

828
48:41.398 --> 48:44.109
Do you happen to remember our live-in maid?

829
48:45.694 --> 48:47.029
The maid…

830
48:48.989 --> 48:49.823
I remember her.

831
48:49.906 --> 48:51.491
So you remember her.

832
48:53.243 --> 48:54.786
Her English is quite good.

833
48:56.038 --> 48:59.124
She's very bright. She can handle the job with no problem.

834
48:59.207 --> 49:02.878
It would be wonderful if she could work at the Government-General

835
49:02.961 --> 49:07.049
and assist with the Commission's visit alongside me.

836
49:07.841 --> 49:10.302
Wouldn't that benefit us both?

837
49:14.556 --> 49:15.390
I was wondering…

838
49:25.233 --> 49:27.069
That's right. She's my girl.

839
49:29.196 --> 49:31.156
That explains it.

840
49:48.924 --> 49:51.259
First a pickpocket, then a live-in maid,

841
49:52.260 --> 49:54.179
now a Government-General's interpreter trainee.

842
49:55.514 --> 49:56.807
What is all this about?

843
49:56.890 --> 49:58.642
I'm trying to make a living.

844
49:58.725 --> 50:00.936
The Governor-General job pays very well.

845
50:20.997 --> 50:22.582
Yeah, I figured.

846
50:22.666 --> 50:26.419
So you know a few words of English, and you want to play the career woman.

847
50:57.450 --> 50:59.035
Need I say more?

848
51:00.620 --> 51:02.747
I assumed you'd know that much.

849
51:04.166 --> 51:08.420
Who would keep their lover in the same office, right next to them?

850
51:08.503 --> 51:09.754
They'd get caught in no time.

851
51:14.259 --> 51:17.762
Ms. Keum, have you ever told anything that was actually true?

852
51:18.346 --> 51:19.181
What?

853
51:19.264 --> 51:22.142
I'm asking if you've ever been honest, even just once.

854
51:23.101 --> 51:24.644
Of course I have.

855
51:24.728 --> 51:26.771
Do you think I lie all the time?

856
51:26.855 --> 51:28.148
Isn't that another lie?

857
51:29.649 --> 51:32.319
You really don't trust people, do you?

858
51:32.402 --> 51:33.820
Can you blame me?

859
51:34.696 --> 51:37.199
Think about everything you've done to me.

860
51:39.743 --> 51:40.577
Ms. Keum.

861
51:41.870 --> 51:44.080
This is the fourth time we have met.

862
51:44.164 --> 51:45.749
First at Gyeongseong Station,

863
51:45.832 --> 51:48.168
then at Mr. Yoo Philip's house.

864
51:48.251 --> 51:50.754
The third was at The First Jongno Pawnshop.

865
51:50.837 --> 51:52.672
Let's chalk those up to coincidence.

866
51:52.756 --> 51:54.549
But the fourth time can't be a coincidence.

867
51:56.593 --> 51:57.844
You asked Mr. Yoo

868
51:57.928 --> 52:00.639
to join the Government-General, in my division, of all places.

869
52:03.391 --> 52:04.351
I give you my word.

870
52:05.143 --> 52:08.897
If you're honest with me just once, without deceiving me,

871
52:10.106 --> 52:11.691
I'll consider you my colleague.

872
52:12.234 --> 52:16.529
Why did you go through Mr. Yoo to come to the Government-General?

873
52:21.034 --> 52:22.869
Why do you keep getting involved with me?

874
52:27.082 --> 52:28.458
I knew you'd have nothing to say.

875
52:29.251 --> 52:30.126
I like you.

876
52:33.755 --> 52:36.341
I've had feelings for you since we first met.

877
52:39.594 --> 52:42.055
That's why I came here.

878
52:55.527 --> 52:58.655
Now, will you consider me your colleague?

879
53:01.283 --> 53:02.617
You're surprisingly easy to fool.

880
53:03.410 --> 53:04.452
Sorry?

881
53:05.453 --> 53:06.579
That was a lie.

882
53:07.414 --> 53:10.041
You're not the only one who can lie.

883
53:12.294 --> 53:14.087
You're a really good liar.

884
53:14.170 --> 53:17.215
I almost fell for it back then too.

885
53:18.008 --> 53:18.925
The princess?

886
53:19.592 --> 53:21.428
The day you stole my wallet?

887
53:31.604 --> 53:35.275
If you lay a hand on me, you can forget about finding it.

888
53:40.030 --> 53:43.199
Wait, did you think I was going to hit you?

889
53:45.160 --> 53:47.329
What kind of person do you take me for?

890
53:47.412 --> 53:48.705
Give me the pawn ticket.

891
53:48.788 --> 53:49.998
Otherwise,

892
53:50.582 --> 53:52.208
I'll tell Mr. Yoo all about this.

893
53:54.210 --> 53:55.378
About what?

894
53:55.462 --> 53:57.672
What you just said to me.

895
54:01.009 --> 54:03.303
What did I just say?

896
54:04.971 --> 54:06.222
Don't you remember?

897
54:06.306 --> 54:08.725
Do you go around saying such things to anyone?

898
54:08.808 --> 54:11.728
I don't say that to just anybody. I said it to you.

899
54:12.645 --> 54:13.897
For the first time in my life.

900
54:17.484 --> 54:21.112
You said if I was honest with you, you'd consider me your colleague.

901
54:21.196 --> 54:22.364
That's why I said it.

902
54:24.824 --> 54:27.327
You said you'd tell Mr. Yoo what I said.

903
54:32.165 --> 54:35.960
It looks like you really believed me.

904
54:49.015 --> 54:50.683
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee.

905
54:53.311 --> 54:54.729
Good to see you again.

906
54:57.899 --> 55:00.193
I'll give it my all, sir.

907
55:00.276 --> 55:02.529
It will be an honor to serve you.

908
55:10.787 --> 55:11.788
Yamada.

909
55:16.584 --> 55:18.294
It's my schedule for next week.

910
55:18.378 --> 55:20.171
-Have a look. -Yes, sir.

911
55:22.841 --> 55:24.134
It's your first day.

912
55:25.468 --> 55:27.303
Did you get a tour of the Government-General?

913
55:33.476 --> 55:36.312
This is the Governor-General's Office, that's the main conference room.

914
55:37.480 --> 55:38.314
Main…

915
55:39.023 --> 55:40.275
This is the supply room.

916
55:40.358 --> 55:42.402
Sorry? Supply…

917
55:42.485 --> 55:43.862
INSPECTOR GENERAL'S OFFICE

918
55:43.945 --> 55:46.197
This is the Inspector General's Office.

919
55:46.281 --> 55:47.407
Inspector General…

920
55:48.491 --> 55:49.367
Hurry up.

921
56:00.462 --> 56:01.921
Have you never seen an elevator?

922
56:41.628 --> 56:43.296
LADIES' ROOM

923
56:43.379 --> 56:44.923
The ladies' room is here.

924
56:56.851 --> 56:57.685
NO ENTRY

925
57:16.371 --> 57:20.166
I'm following this plan because I trust you, not her.

926
57:20.750 --> 57:23.711
I don't completely trust her either. And I shouldn't.

927
57:24.420 --> 57:26.297
So we should keep Suzuki's identity,

928
57:26.381 --> 57:28.883
or that we're a fake married couple, to ourselves.

929
57:29.592 --> 57:31.803
Okay, but she'll definitely put us in danger.

930
57:33.179 --> 57:34.472
Probably.

931
57:35.848 --> 57:37.684
But Ga-kyung will do fine.

932
57:37.767 --> 57:39.978
I'm talking about you, not her.

933
57:45.400 --> 57:48.027
To be honest, I don't care what happens to her.

934
57:48.111 --> 57:50.613
What matters to me is you, So-ran.

935
57:57.662 --> 58:00.665
Dae-seong!

936
58:01.624 --> 58:02.584
It's time to eat!

937
58:02.667 --> 58:04.043
-Okay! -Okay!

938
58:06.462 --> 58:08.840
You're supposed to hurry home when it's time.

939
58:22.437 --> 58:24.689
What did Ga-kyung give us?

940
58:24.772 --> 58:26.566
QUICK RELIEF FOR KIDS' CONSTIPATION

941
58:26.649 --> 58:28.276
I don't know what it says.

942
58:36.868 --> 58:38.244
And what's this drawing?

943
58:39.495 --> 58:40.330
Feed the flowers

944
58:41.539 --> 58:42.707
with manure?

945
58:42.790 --> 58:44.542
Ga-kyung.

946
58:45.126 --> 58:47.211
Don't go.

947
58:56.596 --> 58:58.723
Did Ga-kyung really go to America?

948
58:58.806 --> 59:00.308
Without even telling us?

949
59:07.607 --> 59:09.776
Did she think I'd be happy getting a bike?

950
59:10.652 --> 59:12.111
She could've at least said goodbye.

951
59:15.031 --> 59:16.699
She shouldn't have left at all.

952
59:34.300 --> 59:36.052
Get the inspector general's schedule.

953
01:00:02.078 --> 01:00:04.372
Excuse me, I'm not going to steal anything.

954
01:00:05.581 --> 01:00:08.960
Have you heard the saying that a guilty conscience needs no accuser?

955
01:00:16.718 --> 01:00:17.844
I'll see you tomorrow.

956
01:00:40.742 --> 01:00:42.952
Why bother locking it? It's pointless anyway.

957
01:00:55.965 --> 01:00:56.799
There.

958
01:01:08.269 --> 01:01:10.521
Whatever. It's not even funny.

959
01:01:21.783 --> 01:01:22.909
I'm not stealing it.

960
01:01:22.992 --> 01:01:25.036
I'm just going to copy it.

961
01:01:25.119 --> 01:01:27.038
INSPECTOR GENERAL'S SCHEDULE

962
01:01:32.585 --> 01:01:33.878
What? She likes me?

963
01:01:35.129 --> 01:01:37.256
It must be nice to say that so easily.

964
01:02:00.696 --> 01:02:03.282
Give it to the man with the lemon in his teacup.

965
01:02:05.618 --> 01:02:07.578
The coffee is on the house.

966
01:02:08.871 --> 01:02:11.207
The bill says it's on the house.

967
01:02:17.255 --> 01:02:19.924
Thank you. Arigato.

968
01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:22.969
Right back at you. Arigato.

969
01:02:23.928 --> 01:02:25.054
Come visit more often.

970
01:02:35.106 --> 01:02:36.691
That was easy.

971
01:02:43.489 --> 01:02:44.448
Freeze.

972
01:02:46.158 --> 01:02:47.994
You're a spy, aren't you?

973
01:02:50.580 --> 01:02:51.581
Keum Seo-hee.

974
01:02:52.623 --> 01:02:54.584
No, I mean, Lee Ga-kyung.

975
01:03:45.426 --> 01:03:49.347
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

976
01:03:51.557 --> 01:03:53.184
Don't worry about her.

977
01:03:53.267 --> 01:03:54.644
She's desperate to go to America.

978
01:03:54.727 --> 01:03:56.145
Who's behind this?

979
01:03:56.228 --> 01:03:57.855
So she won't betray us easily.

980
01:03:58.773 --> 01:04:01.233
Your wrists, the bruises, and ankles.

981
01:04:01.317 --> 01:04:03.027
Did he do that to you?

982
01:04:03.110 --> 01:04:05.363
According to the schedule you copied,

983
01:04:05.446 --> 01:04:06.906
at 7:00 p.m. on Monday…

984
01:04:06.989 --> 01:04:09.408
Joseon women are bound to betray us.

985
01:04:09.492 --> 01:04:11.702
She's the one who copied the schedule.

986
01:04:12.286 --> 01:04:13.996
Don't let Mr. Yoo find out.

987
01:04:14.080 --> 01:04:16.415
We have to seize the opportunity when it comes.

988
01:04:16.499 --> 01:04:19.710
If you put her in danger, you won't be safe either.

989
01:04:27.426 --> 01:04:29.428
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
